# Soap dish 0: a 10 x 7 cm cream ceramic soap dish at 30 times life size, only its RIM (the floor inside is the room's floor): 30 m long (x) and 21 m wide (z), the rim 1.2 m tall
# and 1.5 m thick, rounded on top, the outside steep (vertical at the foot) with corners of 6 m radius. Three gaps cut through the rim are the gates:
#   - the MAIN gate, 4 m wide, in the middle of the +z long side (local x 0, z +10.5). It faces local +z, so the level places it at yaw 90 on the west side (+z becomes +x, towards
#     the middle) and at yaw -90 on the east side.
#   - two end gates, 2.5 m wide, in the middle of the two short sides (local x -15 and +15, z 0); at yaw 90 these are world z +15 and -15 (north and south).
# Origin at the middle on y = 0 (no floor, so the stand and pods sit on the room's floor). Mesh collider.
format 1
collider mesh

# The rim's outer solid: a rounded plan 30 x 21, the top edge rounded, the foot cut flat at the floor
outer =
    Intersection
        Translate translation=(0, 0.3, 0)
            Elongate amount=(9, 0, 4.5)
                RoundedCylinder radius=6 roundness=0.6 height=0.93
        Translate translation=(0, 1.2, 0)
            Box size=(20, 1.2, 15)

# The inside of the dish, 1.5 m in from the outside, going through the floor
inner =
    Translate translation=(0, 0.5, 0)
        Elongate amount=(9, 0, 4.5)
            RoundedCylinder radius=4.5 roundness=0.2 height=2

# One end gate, mirrored to the other end
endGate =
    Translate translation=(15, 0.6, 0)
        Box size=(2, 1.5, 1.25)

Detail detail=0.5
    Material material=bath_ceramic
        Subtraction
            Subtraction
                SmoothSubtraction smoothness=0.25
                    $outer
                    $inner
                # The main gate
                Translate translation=(0, 0.6, 10.5)
                    Box size=(2, 1.5, 2)
            SymmetryX
                $endGate
